{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 37, :comments ["<b>Also with me was YHWH angered because of you.</b> He says: Behold, your sin that you committed at that time with the spies withheld from you the good land, and you further added to sin on another occasion, until you withheld even me from crossing. For he wanted to mention together the punishment of all those who were prevented from crossing into the land, because it was all caused by their sins. And so that he might mention here the matter of Joshua — for he will cross because he fully followed YHWH, unlike his counterpart — and that he would further merit to bequeath the land to the second generation, since Moses was punished and it was decreed upon him that he would not cross. Now, he mentioned the entire episode except for the plague of the spies themselves, and he also did not mention the evil report, for he does not speak in disparagement of individuals, but rather reproves the congregation as a whole — that all of them sinned and all of them were punished. And the sense of <i>because of you</i> is as it says, the children of Israel contended with YHWH, etc. (Numbers 20:13), and all this happened because of your contention. Or he may hint that the anger was upon Moses and upon Aaron, when they struck the rock twice before the people and did not do as they were commanded, and the people reflected upon the matter. And this is what He said (Deuteronomy 32:51), because you did not sanctify Me among the children of Israel — that the punishment was only because the matter was among the children of Israel, so that the honor was not sanctified in their eyes. And thus it says in the Sifre (Ha'azinu 50): <i>because you trespassed against Me</i> (there) — you caused the trespassing; <i>because you did not sanctify Me</i> — you caused that I was not sanctified; <i>when you rebelled against My word</i> (Numbers 27:14) — you caused the rebelling against My word. All these expressions are directed against Israel. And I have already explained the matter (in my commentary to Numbers 20:8)."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {0 "The citation (שם כ ח) refers back to Numbers 20:8; Ramban's closing parenthetical points to his earlier commentary on that verse."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T02:44:16.209410913Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}